=== SURVEY ===
Web source components/charts/AreaChartWrapper.tsx is a reusable, purely-presentational gradient area
chart. Props: data (Record[]), xKey (string), series ({ key, label, color }[]), height? (=300),
xFormatter?((string)=>string), yFormatter?((number)=>string), className?. Body:
  • <ResponsiveContainer height={height}><AreaChart data margin>
  • <defs>: one vertical linearGradient per series — stop 0% color@0.30 → stop 100% color@0.00.
  • <CartesianGrid strokeDasharray="3 3"> + <XAxis dataKey=xKey tickFormatter=xFormatter>
    + <YAxis tickFormatter=yFormatter> + <Tooltip> (dark; formatter → [yFormatter(value), series.label];
    labelFormatter = xFormatter).
  • one <Area type="monotone" dataKey stroke=color strokeWidth=2 fill="url(#gradient)"> per series.
The component has NO t() calls (anonymous), NO data hooks, NO loading/empty/error chrome — those belong
to its host. Real call sites (web): RecentActivity battery trend (series #10b981, yFormatter `${v}%`),
ChargeHistoryWidget (series #10b981, yFormatter `${v} kWh`) — both single-series, xKey="i" (row index),
no xFormatter.
Data sources (P1/S8): none (pure presentational — bound here through a host-payload state-holder seam).
Shared components: none. Charts/maps: Recharts AreaChart → Swift Charts AreaMark+LineMark.
i18n keys extracted from source: none (anonymous surface — all native-chrome keys added).
Existing native: no AreaChartWrapper / AreaChart* symbols (grep = 0, no collision). Canonical surface
pattern studied: shared-surfaces/SmallMultiplesChart (Adapter/Projection/Model/Views/Previews/strings/
Tests/AdapterTests/ViewTests) — mirrored here.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is presentational; the prompt requires a production-polished native surface that
  reproduces its DATA, composition, states, and (native-chrome) i18n, with every state visible. Chosen:
  the gradient area chart drawn natively in Swift Charts (per-series unstacked monotone AreaMark with a
  0.30→0.00 vertical LinearGradient fill + a 2pt monotone LineMark stroke — the verbatim parity of the
  web <Area> gradient + strokeWidth) over a token-styled cartesian grid with formatted x/y axes (web
  XAxis/YAxis tickFormatter) and a drag-scrub cursor read-out (web <Tooltip>) — wrapped in the P4 leaf
  contract the standalone web component leaves to its host.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical SmallMultiplesChart leaf:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AreaChartResolve; AreaChartSeries (web {key,label,color}); AreaChartRow
    (web data[i] = xKey value + per-series numbers); AreaChartPoint (finite (index,value)); AreaValueFormat
    (web yFormatter — suffix + fraction digits + abbreviate); AreaLabelFormat (web xFormatter — verbatim/
    truncate); AreaChartConnection/Availability/EmptyBehavior/Input/Meta; AreaChartProjector (per-series
    finite-only projection + x labels); AreaChartFormat (number/label); AreaChartPalette (#rrggbb decoder);
    AreaChartAccessibility (VoiceOver summary builders).
  • Projection: AreaChartSeriesRow / AreaChartPlot / AreaChartFreshness / AreaChartEmpty /
    AreaChartErrorContent / AreaChartResolved(+Phase, presentsContent); AreaChartProjection.resolve —
    loading / error / empty / withdrawn / populated, multi-series mapping, y-formatter → spoken summary,
    freshness axis.
  • Model: AreaChartTelemetry seam (+ OSLog default); AreaChartSource seam + Live/InMemory sources;
    @Observable AreaChartWrapperModel (binds the source, emits view.opened once on first content, one-shot
    stale auto-refresh); AreaChartWrapperStrings i18n facade.
  • Views: Swift Charts canvas (areaMarks/lineMarks/selectionMarks, x/y AxisMarks, scrub gesture, tooltip),
    freshness chip, loading skeleton, empty (ContentUnavailableView), error (retry), populated container.
  • main surface + Previews + strings + Tests/AdapterTests/ViewTests.
- States rendered (every one — no hidden surface, no blank box): loading (TSSkeleton), error (retry — web
  QueryError peer), empty (ContentUnavailableView, the P4 stand-in for the web host hiding the region),
  withdrawn (EmptyView — the host-hidden collapse), populated (the area chart), plus the orthogonal
  connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/recharts literally (used Swift Charts + P1/S9 tokens); closure-typed
  x/yFormatter props (modelled declaratively as AreaValueFormat/AreaLabelFormat so the projection stays
  pure + Equatable + testable); HTTP/data-fetch in the view (bound via the source seam); a truly
  invisible surface (P4 forbids blank boxes — every state renders real content).

